\b Final Web Project Proposal\b0\par
\par
\b Project Title & Summary\b0\par
StudySprint AI is a web-based study planner and focus assistant that helps students organize coursework, generate personalized study sessions, and stay accountable with smart reminders. The app combines a clean task dashboard with AI-powered recommendations and real-time productivity insights, turning scattered assignments and deadlines into a structured weekly plan that is easy to follow on desktop and mobile.\par
\par
\b Purpose & Goals\b0\par
The project solves a common student problem: feeling overwhelmed by multiple deadlines and not knowing what to study first. It demonstrates how modern web apps can combine interactive UI, external APIs, and AI features to create practical, user-centered tools. Goals include improving time management, reducing procrastination, and showcasing full-stack-ready frontend skills such as state management, asynchronous API integration, and responsive design.\par
\par
\b Features\b0\par
\bullet Assignment and exam tracker with priority tags, due dates, and completion states.\par
\bullet AI study plan generator that suggests what to work on each day based on urgency and estimated effort.\par
\bullet “Explain this topic” AI helper for quick concept breakdowns in simpler language.\par
\bullet Calendar view with drag-and-drop rescheduling.\par
\bullet Pomodoro focus timer with session history and streak tracking.\par
\bullet Local notifications/reminders for upcoming deadlines.\par
\bullet Optional weather-based study tip using a weather API (e.g., suggest indoor deep-work sessions on rainy days).\par
\bullet Data persistence with local storage (and optional cloud sync in a future version).\par
\par
\b Tools & Frameworks\b0\par
\bullet Frontend: HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript (ES6+)\par
\bullet UI Framework: React + Vite\par
\bullet Styling: Tailwind CSS\par
\bullet APIs/Integrations: OpenAI API (AI planner + concept helper), OpenWeather API (context tips)\par
\bullet PWA Features: Service worker, installable app manifest, offline support for previously loaded tasks\par
\bullet Version Control: Git + GitHub\par
\par
\b Deployment Plan\b0\par
The project will be deployed on Vercel for fast CI/CD from GitHub, automatic preview deployments, and easy production rollbacks. The repository will remain public on GitHub, and each push to the main branch will trigger a new production build.\par
}
